    {
      "number": "1.0",
      "title": "1.0 SCOPE",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 113,
      "text_length": 181,
      "text_preview": "This Software Requirements Specification (SRS) identifies the requirements for the ASPERA-3 Processing and Archiving Facility (APAF) ground data system for the Mars Express mission."
    },
    {
      "number": "1.1",
      "title": "1.1 Project Identification",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 117,
      "text_length": 829,
      "text_preview": "<table><tr><td rowspan=1 colspan=1>Project Title:</td><td rowspan=1 colspan=1>ASPERA for Mars Express</td></tr><tr><td rowspan=1 colspan=1>Project Number:</td><td rowspan=1 colspan=1>15-02853 / 15-035"
    },
    {
      "number": "1.2",
      "title": "1.2 Data System Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 121,
      "text_length": 1930,
      "text_preview": "The ASPERA-3 instrument package (or ASPERA-3 experiment) will be flown on the Mars Express mission of the European Space Agency (ESA) and will be launched in June 2003 according to the current schedul"
    },
    {
      "number": "1.3",
      "title": "1.3 Goals and Objectives",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 145,
      "text_length": 461,
      "text_preview": "The APAF ground data system is to provide data processing algorithms and support to IRF for the ASPERA-3 science team (including Co-I’s) in preparation for the Mission Operations and Data Analysis (MO"
    },
    {
      "number": "1.4",
      "title": "1.4 Document Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 149,
      "text_length": 378,
      "text_preview": "Section 2 is an overview of the descriptions of requirement determination, qualification procedures, rationale, and traceability that are used in the identification and the definitions of the requirem"
    },
    {
      "number": "1.5",
      "title": "1.5 Related Documents",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 153,
      "text_length": 1535,
      "text_preview": "Program-Level Requirements for the ASPERA-3 Mission of Opportunity Project: approved Nov. 1999   \nAPAF Software Development Plan: APAF-SDP-15-02853, Version 1.2 released November 27, 2000   \nAPAF Proj"
    },
    {
      "number": "2.0",
      "title": "2.0 REQUIREMENTS SPECIFICATION DESCRIPTIONS",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 173,
      "text_length": 0,
      "text_preview": ""
    },
    {
      "number": "2.1",
      "title": "2.1 Requirement Identification",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 175,
      "text_length": 325,
      "text_preview": "Each requirement shall be:\n\n• Necessary: It states a condition for the acceptance of the system.\n\n• Verifiable: It is stated in such a way that an objective test can be defined for it.\n\n• Attainable: "
    },
    {
      "number": null,
      "title": "Each requirement shall be:",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 187,
      "text_length": 246,
      "text_preview": "• assigned a project-unique identifier.\n\n• annotated with associated qualification (verification) methods (see section 2.2).\n\nannotated with rationale (see section 2.3).\n\n• annotated with associated t"
    },
    {
      "number": "2.2",
      "title": "2.2 Qualification Provisions",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 197,
      "text_length": 826,
      "text_preview": "For each requirement in Section 3, the method(s) to be used to verify that the requirement has been met is annotated. Qualification methods included in this specification are:\n\n• Demonstration: observ"
    },
    {
      "number": "2.3",
      "title": "2.3 Rationale",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 205,
      "text_length": 282,
      "text_preview": "The rationale behind each requirement is documented, if applicable, in Section 3 along with each requirement. Rationale may include:\n\n• assumptions\n\n• why a requirement is needed\n\n• how a requirement "
    },
    {
      "number": "2.4",
      "title": "2.4 Requirements Traceability",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 217,
      "text_length": 678,
      "text_preview": "The relationship between each requirement and the project item(s) that it addresses is documented along with each requirement identified in Section 3. A requirement may address any number of project i"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.0",
      "title": "3.0 REQUIREMENTS",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 229,
      "text_length": 145,
      "text_preview": "The APAF ground data system requirements are categorized according to functional areas and are defined in the following sections in table format."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.1",
      "title": "3.1 Capability or Functional Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 233,
      "text_length": 6394,
      "text_preview": "The requirements associated with the functionality of the APAF ground data system are itemized in the table below. The mnemonic, FR, is used in the requirement identifiers to show that these requireme"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.2",
      "title": "3.2 External Interface Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 239,
      "text_length": 3666,
      "text_preview": "The requirements associated with external interfaces of the APAF data system are identified and described in the APAF Data System Interface Document (APAF-DSID-15-03561-V1.0). For ease of reference, t"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.3",
      "title": "3.3 Internal Interface Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 252,
      "text_length": 194,
      "text_preview": "All internal interfaces are left to the design. The Software Design Documents of each of the seven components (see section 1.2) shall contain the detailed information of the internal interfaces."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.4",
      "title": "3.4 Internal Data Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 256,
      "text_length": 211,
      "text_preview": "All internal data requirements are left to the design. The Software Design Documents of each of the seven components (see section 1.2) shall contain the detailed information of the virtual instrument "
    },
    {
      "number": "3.5",
      "title": "3.5 Security and Privacy Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 260,
      "text_length": 1012,
      "text_preview": "There are no security requirements associated with the APAF ground data system. However, there are privacy issues related to intellectual property and sensitive information and data. The requirement a"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.6",
      "title": "3.6 Computer Resource Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 266,
      "text_length": 1847,
      "text_preview": "The requirements associated with computer resources are listed in the table below. Computer resources include computer hardware, computer software, and computer communication. The mnemonic, CR, is use"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.7",
      "title": "3.7 Logistics-Related Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 272,
      "text_length": 1181,
      "text_preview": "The SwRI software team shall provide system maintenance and software support.\n\nThe logistics-related requirements of the APAF ground data system are itemized in the following table. The mnemonic, LR, "
    },
    {
      "number": "3.8",
      "title": "3.8 Delivery Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 280,
      "text_length": 6299,
      "text_preview": "The APAF data system requirements for delivering the ASPERA-3 IDFS data, Mars Express Orbit/Attitude IDFS data, and software are described in the following table. The mnemonic, DR, is used in the requ"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9",
      "title": "3.9 Other Requirements Considered",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 286,
      "text_length": 109,
      "text_preview": "This section identifies the requirements considered but not part of the APAF ground data system requirements."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.1",
      "title": "3.9.1 Required States and Modes",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 290,
      "text_length": 79,
      "text_preview": "The APAF data system is not required to operate in more than one state or mode."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.2",
      "title": "3.9.2 Adaptation Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 294,
      "text_length": 192,
      "text_preview": "There are no installation-dependent requirements for the operation of the APAF data system. However, if any are identified, they shall be documented in the APAF Operations Procedures Document."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.3",
      "title": "3.9.3 Safety Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 298,
      "text_length": 164,
      "text_preview": "The APAF data system will not impose hazards to personnel, property, or the environment. Therefore, there are no safety requirements of the APAF ground data system."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.4",
      "title": "3.9.4 Software Quality Factors",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 302,
      "text_length": 370,
      "text_preview": "Although the APAF data system and associated software will be developed with the highest quality possible, there are no requirements concerned with software quality. Some of the software quality facto"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.5",
      "title": "3.9.5 Design and Implementation Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 306,
      "text_length": 92,
      "text_preview": "There are no requirements that constrain the design and implementation of the APAF software."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.6",
      "title": "3.9.6 Personnel-Related Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 310,
      "text_length": 196,
      "text_preview": "There are no identified requirements related to personnel that will use the software. However, the APAF Operations Procedures Document will aid personnel in the operational use of the APAF system."
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.7",
      "title": "3.9.7 Training-Related Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 314,
      "text_length": 442,
      "text_preview": "Since the members of the SwRI software team are experienced with data system and IDFS processing software development, there are no training-related requirements for developers of the APAF data system"
    },
    {
      "number": "3.9.8",
      "title": "3.9.8 Precedence and Criticality of Requirements",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 320,
      "text_length": 108,
      "text_preview": "There are no requirements of the APAF data system that need special treatment or consideration at this time."
    },
    {
      "number": "4.0",
      "title": "4.0 NOTES",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 324,
      "text_length": 430,
      "text_preview": "To aid in the understanding of this specification, the requirements imposed on SwRI for the development and operation of the ASPERA-3 Mission of Opportunity (MO) of the NASA Discovery Program as they "
    },
    {
      "number": null,
      "title": "In Section 4.1.1, Baseline Science Requirements, it states:",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 328,
      "text_length": 783,
      "text_preview": "“…the ASPERA-3 MO shall provide the complete data set of the integrated ASPERA-3 investigation to all ASPERA-3 Co-I’s and the NASA Planetary Data System (PDS). The specific measurements delivered shal"
    },
    {
      "number": null,
      "title": "In Section 4.3, Launch Requirements, it states:",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 343,
      "text_length": 158,
      "text_preview": "“…data processing software shall meet the delivery requirements of the IRF in order to support the launch date and operation of the ESA Mars Express mission.”"
    },
    {
      "number": null,
      "title": "In Section 4.4, Ground System Requirements, it states:",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 347,
      "text_length": 694,
      "text_preview": "“SwRI shall develop the ASPERA-3 data reduction system and software to be used during instrument integration, test, calibration and mission operations for the full ASPERA-3 experiment. This task will "
    },
    {
      "number": null,
      "title": "In Section 4.5.1, Science Data Management, it states:",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 353,
      "text_length": 428,
      "text_preview": "“…the ASPERA-3 MO PI shall be responsible for collecting engineering and ancillary information necessary to validate and calibrate the scientific data prior to depositing it in the NASA PDS in a PDS-c"
    },
    {
      "number": null,
      "title": "In Section 4.5.2, Analysis Software, it states:",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 357,
      "text_length": 229,
      "text_preview": "“Science analysis software developed by the ASPERA-3 MO PI team for this project shall be integrated into the NASA approved data repository. The PI team and the science community shall have equal on-l"
    },
    {
      "number": null,
      "title": "In Section 4.5.3, Data Management Plan, it states:",
      "level": 2,
      "line_start": 361,
      "text_length": 591,
      "text_preview": "“The ASPERA-3 MO Project shall develop a project data management plan to address the total activity associated with the flow of science data, including planning, acquisition, processing, data product "
    }
